## Open formats already implemented

PCM/WAV, FLAC, Opus, Vorbis, AV1, and VP9 are open standards. They
are implemented in software in this library with no license gate.
(AV1 and VP9 are parser-only in Phases 7–8: headers and tile
framing parse; pixel reconstruction returns `Unsupported`.)

## H.264/AVC, H.265/HEVC, AAC — behind a license gate

H.264/AVC, H.265/HEVC, and AAC are patent-encumbered codecs. This
library contains **no software encoder or decoder for AVC or
HEVC**, and never will: `Decoder::decode` and `Encoder::encode`
refuse `Codec::Avc` and `Codec::Hevc` outright. The only path is
the hardware path in `crates/codec-whatttttttttttt-core/src/hw.rs`
(`HardwareDecoder` / `HardwareEncoder`, currently a stub that
calls no real hardware API), opened with a caller-supplied
`LicenseContext` (`crates/codec-whatttttttttttt-core/src/license.rs`).

AAC is different: AAC-LC has a software decoder
(`Decoder::from_aac_config` in
`crates/codec-whatttttttttttt-core/src/decoder.rs`), allowed only
when the `licensed-aac` feature is on and a valid `LicenseContext`
was presented and validated at construction. Without a license
the software path returns the gate error
(`Error::Unsupported` when the feature is off,
`Error::LicenseRequired` when it is on). There is no software
AAC encoder in this library; `Encoder::encode` for `Codec::Aac`
returns the same gate error.

The gate is **off by default**. It is controlled by the Cargo
features `licensed-avc-hevc` and `licensed-aac` in
`crates/codec-whatttttttttttt-core/Cargo.toml` (`default = []`):

- Feature off: the licensed path is not compiled in, and the
  software path returns `Error::Unsupported`.
- Feature on, no valid license presented: the path exists and is
  closed, and the error is `Error::LicenseRequired { codec }`
  (C ABI code `CODEC_ERR_LICENSE_REQUIRED = 8`).
- A malformed license is `Error::InvalidArgument`; an expired
  license is `Error::LicenseRequired`.

There is a `Codec::Aac` variant. The `licensed-aac` feature
gates both the AAC-LC software decode path
(`Decoder::from_aac_config`) and the hardware path in `hw.rs`.

The gate is a compliance mechanism only. It checks the shape of
a caller-supplied license (id format, expiry) and records an
in-memory audit log; it performs no online verification, holds
no key, and cannot establish the legal standing of a license.
**It does not replace a real patent license, and it is not legal
advice.** The caller is responsible for obtaining whatever
patent licenses apply, from the relevant patent pools, before
enabling the features or using the hardware path.

## MP3 — not implemented; patent status needs verification

MP3 is **not implemented** in this library (no MP3 encode or
decode in any phase so far). If MP3 support is added in a later
phase, its current patent status must be verified first:
"cần xác minh tình trạng bằng sáng chế hiện tại" — do not assume
from this file that MP3 is unencumbered, and do not add MP3 code
until that check has been done and recorded here.

## ALAC — implemented from Apple's open-source reference (Apache-2.0)

ALAC is implemented in software in this library
(`crates/codec-whatttttttttttt-core/src/alac_frame.rs` and
`src/alac_predictor.rs`: magic-cookie parsing, frame elements,
adaptive Rice decode, LPC predictor, channel decorrelation),
with no license gate. The implementation follows Apple's
open-source ALAC reference implementation, published by Apple
under the Apache License 2.0
(<https://github.com/macosforge/alac>); the algorithm was
re-implemented in Rust from that published source, which is the
attribution this file carries. ALAC encode is not implemented
yet; `Encoder::encode` for `Codec::Alac` returns
`Error::Unsupported`.

## No other patented codecs

No other patent-encumbered codec is implemented or planned in
this round. Any future codec addition must record its patent /
license status in this file before its code lands.
